  "narrative": "All newly delivered estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support the registered association and negative signed values oppose it. The PTEN-loss/STAT3 association continues to look robust across several contexts, but the context checks are not equally secure. H105, the KY-library stratum, is positive and interval-excluding-zero (+0.158, 95% CI +0.063 to +0.254; R101), but the exposed cell count is modest (64) and the lower bound is below my preferred practical threshold of about 0.10 on the dependency-score scale. Because this is a moderate context-specific effect and many assay/co-mutation contexts have been tested, I accept it as a dataset association for now but request independent validation of H105. This is the most useful validation target among the new results because it has the greatest remaining uncertainty among the accepted context checks. H106, the KEAP1-loss stratum, is large and precise (+0.247, 95% CI +0.133 to +0.361; R102), so I accept and close it without validation. H109 extends the MSI-high/WRN association to the KY library (+0.732, 95% CI +0.675 to +0.790; R105); despite only 32 exposed cases, the effect is enormous relative to the WRN score scale and the interval is far above zero, so I accept and close it without validation. H105 is therefore the single new validation request.\n\nThe interaction and specificity probes are mostly null. H97 tests whether PTEN-loss/STAT3 is modified by KRAS mutation; the signed interaction is small and opposite to the hypothesized stronger effect (-0.024, 95% CI -0.148 to +0.100; R94). Given the imprecision and lack of a signal, I reject and close it. H107 and H108 show that PTEN loss is not meaningfully associated with USP7 or MDM2 dependency, supporting the STAT3-specificity of the PTEN-loss association rather than broad p53/MDM2-axis pleiotropy. The new mechanistic probes are also unsupported: PIK3CA mutation is not associated with stronger STAT3 or weaker EGFR dependency; STK11 loss is not meaningfully associated with stronger STAT3; MTAP loss in TP53-intact cells shows an opposite/nonsignificant MDM2 contrast; and TP53-intact status is not associated with stronger STAT3. These effects are small, interval-crossing, or directionally opposite, so I reject and close them.\n\nI also reassess the EGFR-amplification/EGFR-dependency claims. The main contrast and clean-context contrasts were borderline but imprecise, and the new direct adenocarcinoma check in H99 is again weak (+0.020, 95% CI -0.010 to +0.049; R95) and not interval-excluding-zero. Across the overall, KRAS-intact, KRAS/PIK3CA-intact, and adenocarcinoma contexts, the estimates remain small and non-significant. I therefore reject and close H5, H14, and H59 as unsupported scientifically meaningful dataset associations for EGFR-amplification effect on EGFR dependency. This does not imply absence of any biological relationship elsewhere, but the supplied dataset does not support a meaningful EGFR-amplification marker association in these analyses.",
  "research_notes": "Current validated or strongly supported dataset associations: (1) MSI-high -> much stronger dependency_WRN, supported overall and in adenocarcinoma, batch_a, Avana, and now KY contexts; (2) SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger dependency_SMARCA2, robust overall and in ARID1A-intact, ARID1A-loss, adenocarcinoma, batch_a, and KY contexts; (3) TP53-intact -> stronger dependency_USP7, validated and robust overall and in KY; (4) KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative dependency_NFE2L2, validated and robust overall, adenocarcinoma, batch_a, and KY; (5) PTEN loss -> stronger dependency_STAT3, validated overall and robust in adenocarcinoma, TP53-intact, TP53-loss, and KEAP1-loss contexts. H105 PTEN/STAT3 KY-library context is accepted provisionally as a moderate context result but independent validation is requested because the lower confidence bound is modest and the exposed cell count is small. If validation confirms, close as validated; if it attenuates, downgrade. New negative findings: PTEN-loss/STAT3 is not modified by KRAS mutation in current data; PTEN loss does not affect USP7 or MDM2 dependency, supporting STAT3 specificity. PIK3CA, STK11, MTAP-in-TP53-intact, and TP53-intact main effects on STAT3 are unsupported. EGFR-amplification main and context checks (overall, KRAS-intact, KRAS/PIK3CA-intact, adenocarcinoma) are weak and non-significant, so H5/H14/H59 are closed as unsupported. Remaining active untested lower-priority claims include H98 PTEN/STAT3 SMAD4 interaction, H73 USP7/TP53 PIK3CA interaction, H25 KRAS in STK11-intact, H30 MYC/POLR2A, and H77 marker_E/WRN. Preserve validation capacity for new large robust discoveries or to confirm moderate accepted contexts. All conclusions remain dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
