  "narrative": "All delivered estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support the registered association and negative signed values oppose it. H85, the main PTEN-loss/STAT3-dependency association, has independently validated: discovery signed effect +0.267 (95% CI +0.215 to +0.320, R73) and validation +0.274 (adjusted CI +0.200 to +0.348, R79). Both point estimates and lower bounds are substantial relative to the STAT3 score scale and the 10% practical-importance threshold, so I keep H85 accepted and closed. H105 tests the same PTEN-loss/STAT3 association in the KY CRISPR library. Discovery was +0.158 (95% CI +0.063 to +0.254, R101), and independent validation was larger at +0.329 (adjusted CI +0.178 to +0.480, R106). Although exposed cell count remains modest, the validated lower bound is positive and above the practical threshold; I accept and close H105 as a robust assay-context result. H89 tested whether PIK3CA mutation modifies PTEN-loss/STAT3 dependency. Discovery interaction was near zero (+0.001, 95% CI -0.150 to +0.152, R83), and validation was slightly opposite and interval-crossing (-0.037, adjusted CI -0.259 to +0.185, R107). There is no evidence for PIK3CA-dependent effect modification, so H89 remains rejected and closed. H67 tested EGFR amplification as a predictor of TMED10 dependency. Discovery was tiny and imprecise (+0.004, 95% CI -0.026 to +0.034, R46), and validation remained small and interval-crossing (+0.013, adjusted CI -0.031 to +0.058, R80); it remains rejected and closed. Overall, the strongest dataset-supported associations are: MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, including ARID1A-intact and ARID1A-loss contexts; TP53-intact status with stronger USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss with weaker or less-negative NFE2L2 dependency; and PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, now validated overall and supported across adenocarcinoma, TP53-intact, TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and KY-library contexts. Negative or null results narrow the scope of these effects: PTEN loss is not associated with USP7 or MDM2 dependency in the tested overall contrast, PIK3CA does not modify PTEN/STAT3, EGFR amplification is not meaningfully associated with EGFR, TMED10, or ERBB2 dependency in the tested analyses, and many co-mutation pathway probes are small or null. Remaining uncertainty is concentrated in smaller untested or underpowered modifiers, especially H98 PTEN/STAT3 interaction with SMAD4 loss, H73 USP7/TP53 interaction with PIK3CA mutation, H25 KRAS mutation in STK11-intact cells for dependency_KRAS, H30 MYC amplification for dependency_POLR2A, and H77 research marker E for WRN. The most informative next analyses are these active context or modifier checks, with validation reserved only if one shows a large, robust discovery signal.",
  "research_notes": "Updated supported dataset associations: (1) MSI-high -> much stronger dependency_WRN: main validated R8/R39 and KY context R105. (2) SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger dependency_SMARCA2: main validated R9/R26; ARID1A-intact R75, ARID1A-loss R65/R66, adenocarcinoma R32, batch_a R29, KY R42. (3) TP53-intact -> stronger dependency_USP7: main validated R12/R40; adenocarcinoma R34, batch_a R30, KY R43/R53. (4) KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative dependency_NFE2L2: main validated R7/R13; adenocarcinoma R33, batch_a R31, KY R44. (5) PTEN loss -> stronger dependency_STAT3: main validated R73/R79; adenocarcinoma R81, TP53-intact R84, TP53-loss R85/R93, KEAP1-loss R102, KY R101/R106. Validated/null modifiers: H89 PIK3CA modification of PTEN/STAT3 is unsupported (R83,R107); H67 EGFR amplification/TMED10 unsupported (R46,R80); H97 KRAS modification of PTEN/STAT3 unsupported (R94); H107/H108 PTEN loss does not affect USP7 or MDM2 in tested overall contrasts. EGFR-amplification/EGFR-dependency claims H5/H14/H59 remain rejected as weak/non-significant. Remaining active lower-priority claims: H98 PTEN/STAT3 SMAD4 interaction, H73 USP7/TP53 PIK3CA interaction, H25 KRAS in STK11-intact, H30 MYC/POLR2A, H77 marker_E/WRN. No new validation requested at this synthesis stage; preserve capacity for a newly discovered large robust effect or newly uncertain accepted association. All conclusions are dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
